# What Cloud Build actually needs is only what the Dockerfile COPYs:
# requirements.txt, ski_optimizer/ and data/. Without this file gcloud
# uploaded the whole working tree -- 47,136 files, 997 MiB, mostly
# .venv (327M), frontend/web/node_modules (714M) and .next (402M) --
# which pushed a build past ten minutes before it even started.
#
# Allowlist rather than blocklist: a new heavy directory should slow
# nobody's deploy by default.
*

!/Dockerfile
!/requirements.txt
!/ski_optimizer/
!/ski_optimizer/**
!/data/
!/data/**

# Never ship these even from inside the allowed paths.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.env
